# Environment variables for HuntMart.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to client code, so any
# variable read through import.meta.env must keep that prefix. Everything
# here ships to the browser bundle. None of these values are secrets:
# Firebase web config and Algolia search-only keys are designed to be
# public. Protect real data with Firebase Security Rules, not by hiding
# these values.

# --- Firebase (required) ---
# Project: e-commerce-app-hunt
# Firebase console > Project settings > General > Your apps > SDK setup
# and configuration. Without these, initializeApp throws and /shop will
# not render at all.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=e-commerce-app-hunt.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=https://e-commerce-app-hunt-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com

# --- Firebase (only needed if Analytics is enabled) ---
# measurementId is optional for firebase-js-sdk v7.20+. Leave both blank
# if you are not collecting analytics.
VITE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_MEASUREMENT_ID=
VITE_APP_ID=

# --- Algolia (required for /shop/search) ---
# App ID and SEARCH-ONLY API key from Algolia > Settings > API keys.
# Never put the Admin/write key here: anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined
# into the client bundle and is readable by anyone who loads the page.
#
# To seed or refresh the index from the records in firebase.json:
#   ALGOLIA_APP_ID=<app-id> ALGOLIA_ADMIN_KEY=<admin-key> \
#     node scripts/seed-algolia.mjs
VITE_ALGOLIA_APP_ID=
VITE_ALGOLIA_SEARCH_KEY=